repository-code: "https://github.com/ANB-007/immigration-microsimulation"
license: MIT
version: 2.1.0
keywords:
  - employment-based immigration
  - per-country cap
  - child age-out
  - microsimulation
abstract: >-
  A petitioner-level microsimulation of the United States employment-based (EB)
  immigration system. It reconstructs the EB green-card queue from FY2009-FY2024,
  assigns dependents using nationality-specific demographic profiles, allocates
  visas under the statutory 7% per-country cap, and projects outcomes through
  FY2040 under the current capped system and an uncapped counterfactual. The
  model quantifies how the per-country cap amplifies and redistributes child
  age-out risk (loss of derivative eligibility at age 21) across national-origin
  groups and EB preference categories. 
